# The pointer ledger is machine-written and committed, and git cannot merge a
# single JSON object. One row per line plus a union merge makes two machines'
# additions combine without a conflict — and "never hand-edited" is unenforceable
# in exactly the situation git would otherwise demand it (design §Reject versus
# flag). Rows are never pruned, which is what makes taking the union sound.
triage/.pointer-ledger.jsonl merge=union
